# [ Claude (Cowork) | Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5) | 2026-08-03 14:52 UTC | edit: stray editor artifacts ]
# An interactive editor session on 2026-08-03 created a default "Untitled" level and its
# World Partition sidecars - 143 files that no phase references and nothing loads. Scoped
# to Untitled deliberately: __ExternalActors__ and __ExternalObjects__ are where a real
# World Partition level would keep its actors, so ignoring those directories wholesale
# would silently stop tracking a future level's content. Delete the files if you want
# them gone; this only stops them appearing as untracked noise on every status.
sandbox/Content/Untitled.umap
sandbox/Content/Untitled_HLOD0_Instancing.uasset
sandbox/Content/__ExternalActors__/Untitled/
sandbox/Content/__ExternalObjects__/Untitled/

# Game Animation Sample: local asset library (Epic content license), 5.9 GB.
# Stays OUT of the repo; selected assets migrate into sandbox/Content deliberately,
# each migration audited (docs/phase0/asset_audits/) and committed on its own.
GameAnimationSample/

# [ Claude (Cowork) | Claude Fable 5 (claude-fable-5) | 2026-08-04 17:32 UTC | edit: Mixamo source library ]
# Mixamo FBX source library (28 clips, audited: docs/phase0/asset_audits/2026-08-04-mixamo-boxing-set.md).
# Mixamo terms permit shipping clips embedded in the game but not redistributing the
# animation files themselves - so the raw FBX never enters the repo. Imported/retargeted
# uassets land in sandbox/Content during the mannequin pass, citing the audit.
mixamo_boxing/

# [ Claude (Cowork) | Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5) | 2026-08-04 17:32 UTC | edit: licensed pack content ]
# PAKPROD "Fighting Animations - Boxing" (Director's Fab purchase) landed in the
# project as 458 MB / 435 files - 382 MB of it 4K demo-mannequin textures. It stays
# OUT of the repo, for two reasons that point the same way: a paid vendor pack is
# not ours to store, and .git is 1.4 MB today. The repo keeps what IS ours - the
# Director code that consumes it, and an audit naming every clip path by name
# (docs/phase0/asset_audits/2026-08-04-pakprod-fighting-animations-boxing.md), so a
# fresh machine restores the dependency from Fab and knows exactly what to expect.
# Nothing here holds authority over the fight: the rendered stream is byte-identical
# with these assets present or absent.
sandbox/Content/BoxingAttacks/
sandbox/Content/__ExternalActors__/BoxingAttacks/
sandbox/Content/__ExternalObjects__/BoxingAttacks/

# [ Claude (Cowork) | Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5) | 2026-08-04 20:15 UTC | edit: Fab imports ]
# Imported Fab exchange-format assets (cartoon arena FBX, boxing glove OBJ). Same
# reasoning as the pack above: vendor content restored from Fab, not stored here.
# What IS ours and IS committed are the import scripts in tools/engine, which
# rebuild this folder from the Vault deterministically, and the audits that name
# every consumed path. The 5,400-tick stream is byte-identical with these assets
# present or absent, so nothing here can be load-bearing.
sandbox/Content/FabImports/

# [ Claude (Cowork) | Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5) | 2026-08-05 03:35 UTC | edit: scratch ]
# Commit-message scratch file. The tool layer strips $ and newlines out of
# PowerShell arguments, so commit bodies are written to a file and passed with
# `git commit -F`. It has shown up as untracked noise in every status since.
_commitmsg.txt

# UE writes one-file-per-actor stubs into the level's external-actor folder on
# every editor open, including for actors the Director spawns at runtime and
# never persists. They carry no authority - the marker stream is byte-identical
# without them - and they churn on every session.
sandbox/Content/__ExternalActors__/

# Research: fetched full text and reconstructed abstracts. Copyright and size
# both say keep these out of git - the committed artifacts are the metadata
# records, the queries, the citations index and the lane syntheses.
research/raw/

